The code statements that lead to the bug are:
x->mode_data = xtfs;
xtfs->x = x;
Reason:
These lines assign the cloned state to x->mode_data before the reorder window allocation. If the allocation of w_saved later fails, xtfs is freed but x->mode_data still points to the freed memory, causing use-after-free when the xfrm clone unwind calls destroy_state().

The code statements that fix the bug are:
x->mode_data = xtfs;
xtfs->x = x;
Reason:
These lines are moved after the successful allocation of the reorder window. If the allocation fails, they are never executed, so x->mode_data remains NULL, and the destroy path safely handles the NULL pointer.

